# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# Angular routes in the browser, so /browse and /auth are not files on disk.
# Without this every route except "/" returns 404 on a static host — every
# deep link, and every page refresh. Verified: /browse and /auth return 404
# on a plain static server without this rule, 200 with it.
#
# This duplicates the rule in the repo-root netlify.toml on purpose. This file
# is copied into the build output as an asset, so routing keeps working even
# if the site's base directory is configured differently in the Netlify UI and
# netlify.toml is never read.
#
# 200 = rewrite, not redirect: the typed URL stays in the address bar so
# Angular can read the route from it.
/*    /index.html   200
